<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Potluck mesh sidecar — macOS ROOT LaunchDaemon.

  This file is embedded STATICALLY, at build time, inside the signed
  Potluck AI.app bundle at Contents/Library/LaunchDaemons/ai.trypotluck.mesh.plist
  (electron-builder's mac.extraFiles — see apps/desktop/electron/package.json).
  It is registered/unregistered at RUNTIME by the mesh-helper Swift CLI
  (apps/desktop/electron/native/mesh-helper/) via
  SMAppService.daemon(plistName: "ai.trypotluck.mesh.plist"), which main.js's
  mesh:enable IPC handler shells out to. See docs/phase-g/local-ipc.md for the
  IPC surface the daemon itself exposes once running.

  WHY THIS FILE CANNOT CONTAIN INSTALL-TIME TOKENS
  --------------------------------------------------
  SMAppService requires the embedded plist to be present, unmodified, inside
  the app's code signature at the moment the app is built and signed — it
  canNOT be rewritten, templated, or regenerated after install (unlike the
  old .pkg-postinstall-rendered template this file replaces, which is now
  dead). Anything that needs to vary per-install (a self-hosted or LAN
  coordinator URL) is handled by a LIVE runtime override instead: a
  PATCH /settings call on the sidecar's local IPC socket persists the
  override to settings.json next to the WireGuard private key (see
  internal/runtimesettings), and the sidecar applies it on every subsequent
  launch BEFORE connecting to any coordinator-facing endpoint. This plist
  only ever carries the PRODUCTION default.

  WHY ROOT (no UserName/GroupName key)
  -------------------------------------
  The WireGuard mesh needs a utun device, which requires root on macOS. We
  deliberately run as a root LaunchDaemon (the same model tailscaled uses)
  rather than requesting the paid Network Extension entitlement, and rather
  than ever prompting the end user for `sudo` — the whole point of the
  SMAppService mechanism is that the user never runs a binary or types a
  password beyond the one-time System Settings > Login Items & Extensions
  approval click.

  The sidecar no longer needs a coordinator token in its environment: a
  pairing token (entered once, in the app's "Add this machine" flow) both
  authorizes enrollment and has the sidecar mint + persist its own per-node
  bearer token on disk (internal/nodetoken) for every later coordinator call.
  Do NOT add POTLUCK_COORDINATOR_TOKEN here.

  --derp-url is the production DERP relay fallback (services/derp,
  fly.toml app=potluck-derp, custom domain derp.trypotluck.ai with its own
  Let's Encrypt cert — Fly terminates TLS on 443 and forwards cleartext to
  the relay binary on 8443, so the client-facing scheme is tcp+tls per
  internal/derp/client.go). Without this flag DERPRelayURL defaults to ""
  (disabled) and cross-network peers with no direct UDP path simply cannot
  connect. Because this flag is passed explicitly here, POTLUCK_DERP_URL
  would NOT override it at runtime (an explicit CLI flag always wins over
  its own env fallback) — an install-specific relay override, if ever
  needed, has to go through the same runtime-settings PATCH /settings
  mechanism described above, not an environment variable.

  KNOWN CONSTRAINT — /Applications only
  ---------------------------------------
  ProgramArguments hardcodes the /Applications install path. Because this
  plist is static, the daemon can only find its own binary if the app is
  installed at the conventional /Applications/Potluck AI.app location (the
  standard outcome of the DMG's drag-to-Applications flow). This is a known,
  shared limitation of every macOS app that ships a privileged LaunchDaemon
  via SMAppService this way — there is no supported way to make an
  SMAppService daemon plist location-independent. If the app is run from
  anywhere else (~/Downloads, a different Applications folder, etc.),
  registration will succeed but launchd will fail to spawn the daemon
  (binary not found at the hardcoded path). Needs an on-device check: see the
  deliverable report for the exact verification steps.

  WG key / signing key / IPC socket paths are intentionally NOT set here —
  the binary's built-in platform defaults apply (internal/config/config.go):
  socket at /tmp/potluck-mesh.sock, keys under
  /var/lib/potluck/mesh/ or $HOME/Library/Application Support/Potluck/mesh/
  depending on what HOME resolves to for this LaunchDaemon's root process.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>ai.trypotluck.mesh</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
      <string>/Applications/Potluck AI.app/Contents/Resources/mesh/potluck-mesh</string>
      <string>--coordinator-url</string>
      <string>https://coordinator.trypotluck.ai</string>
      <!-- Pin the key directory. Under launchd $HOME is unreliable, so the
           $HOME-dependent default would put wg.key / node.token / signing.key
           in shifting locations between runs and desync enrollment state (a
           fresh /pair would 409 already_enrolled). node.token and signing.key
           are co-located with this path (see internal/config Load()). -->
      <string>--wg-private-key-path</string>
      <string>/Library/Application Support/Potluck/mesh/wg.key</string>
      <string>--derp-url</string>
      <string>tcp+tls://derp.trypotluck.ai:443</string>
      <string>--log-format</string>
      <string>json</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Start immediately once registered/approved, and keep it running —
         the mesh daemon must outlive the Electron app entirely (it's a
         member-operated compute network node, not a per-session process). -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- /Library/Logs always exists on a stock macOS install, unlike a
         Potluck-specific subdirectory launchd would need to create itself
         (it does not create missing parent directories for these paths). -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Library/Logs/potluck-mesh.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Library/Logs/potluck-mesh.err</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
